  {% set alosimPrimary = providerB.codes | findCode(providerB.primaryCode) %}

  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      Pick <strong>Holafly</strong> for a flat unlimited price and no gigabyte counting. Pick <strong>AloSIM</strong> if you'd rather pay per GB and want the option of a bundled free international phone number thrown in. AloSIM does also sell its own unlimited plans, so it's not strictly one-or-the-other on data structure; the phone number and the code terms are what actually separate them.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Core Difference: Unlimited-Only vs. Both, Plus a Free Number</h2>
  <p>
    Holafly sells unlimited data as the entire product; there's no fixed-GB option at all. AloSIM sells both fixed-GB plans and its own unlimited plans, so you get to choose the pricing model without switching providers. Where AloSIM adds something Holafly doesn't have any equivalent of: a free international phone number through a partnership with Hushed, set up separately inside the AloSIM app after buying a plan. If you need a number to receive a verification text or give out without handing over your real one, that's a genuine AloSIM-only feature on this comparison.
  </p>
  <p>
    Holafly counters with something AloSIM doesn't offer: a China eSIM with a VPN built in, so Google Maps, WhatsApp, and Gmail work without installing a separate VPN app first. If China is the destination, that's a real point in Holafly's favor regardless of pricing.
  </p>

