    <p style="margin-top:.75rem;margin-bottom:0;color:#63553F;">Holafly's code is ours; AloSIM doesn't run the kind of affiliate program that supports a code like that, so its code is the best public one we've verified. Both apply to repeat purchases, not just a first order.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Is Holafly or AloSIM the Right Pick</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--primary">
      <h3>Go with Holafly if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You genuinely don't know how much data you'll use</li>
        <li>Heavy streaming, video calls, or hotspot use</li>
        <li>China is on the itinerary and you want the built-in VPN</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--secondary">
      <h3>Go with AloSIM if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want a free international number bundled in without adding a separate app</li>
        <li>You'd rather pick between fixed-GB and unlimited from the same checkout</li>
        <li>Light data user who'd rather pay per GB than a flat unlimited rate</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two Things Worth Knowing Before You Decide</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>AloSIM's refund guarantee has a timing catch.</strong> It covers eSIMs that fail to connect or turn out incompatible with the device, not ones activated and simply not used much. Buy ahead if you like (an unused AloSIM eSIM doesn't expire), just don't activate it until you're ready to actually use it. Holafly's plans don't carry the same kind of pre-activation refund window; check the specific plan's terms before buying.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Holafly's "Always On" tier keeps a subscriber connected between trips.</strong> Cancel a Holafly monthly Plans subscription and you're dropped to 1GB a month across 160+ destinations instead of zero, enough to land somewhere and get online without paying for a full plan. AloSIM doesn't have an equivalent standby tier; its plans are simply active or expired.
  </p>
  <p>
    For device setup and eSIM basics that apply to both providers, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>Holafly vs AloSIM FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is cheaper, Holafly or AloSIM</h3>
      <p>Depends on usage. AloSIM's fixed-GB plans are usually cheaper for light data use on a short trip. Holafly's flat unlimited price is usually cheaper, or at least less stressful, for heavy data use.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does either include a phone number</h3>
      <p>AloSIM does, through a partnership with Hushed: a free international number set up inside the AloSIM app after purchase. Holafly has no equivalent feature.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is better for a trip to China</h3>
      <p>Holafly, for travelers who don't want to set up a separate VPN, since its China eSIM includes one built in. AloSIM has no equivalent feature.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does AloSIM also sell unlimited plans like Holafly</h3>
      <p>Yes. AloSIM sells both fixed-GB and unlimited plans, so the choice between the two pricing models is available on AloSIM alone, without needing to compare against Holafly for the unlimited option.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

